##### WhatsAppTemplateRuleSnapshot

`WhatsAppTemplateRuleSnapshot` is a versioned snapshot of the current Meta-related validation rules and limits known by Falcon. It prevents hardcoding Meta limits inside many validators.

Instead of writing this inside rule implementations:

```csharp
if (body.Length > 1024)
```

rules should use the snapshot:

```csharp
if (body.Length > context.Rules.Body.MaxLength)
```

Example snapshot:

```json
{
  "version": "2026.05.10",
  "name": {
    "minLength": 1,
    "maxLength": 215,
    "pattern": "^[a-z0-9_]+$"
  },
  "body": {
    "minLength": 1,
    "maxLength": 1024
  },
  "footer": {
    "maxLength": 60,
    "variablesAllowed": false
  },
  "buttons": {
    "maxButtons": 10,
    "quickReplyTextMaxLength": 25,
    "websiteButtonMaxCount": 2,
    "phoneButtonMaxCount": 1
  },
  "authentication": {
    "copyCodeEnabled": true,
    "oneTapEnabled": false,
    "zeroTapEnabled": false,
    "minOtpExpirySeconds": 30,
    "maxOtpExpirySeconds": 900
  }
}
```

The word `Snapshot` is important because Meta rules may change. Falcon should know which validation rule version was used when a template was validated or submitted. This helps support teams debug cases where a template passed validation under an older rule version but fails after Meta changes its rules.

Recommended naming:

```csharp
public required WhatsAppTemplateRuleSnapshot Rules { get; init; }
```

If Falcon later supports providers beyond Meta WhatsApp, the name can become more generic, such as `ProviderRuleSnapshot`.

