```

This is where your **MicroappOutletComponent** renders the micro-app.

2.  Prevent style classes conflicts, so Micro-apps shouldn’t have global styles.  
    All Micro-apps styles should be scoped under a host-classs


```
:host-context(.microapp-container) .page {
  font-size: 14px;
}
```

3.  Micro-Apps Inherit Layout Styling Automatically  
    Shell sets the root theme:

```
:root {
  --primary-color: #0055ff;
  --padding-base: 16px;
  --layout-content-bg: #ffffff;
}
```

Micro-apps automatically use them:

```
.page-container {
  background: var(--layout-content-bg);
  padding: var(--padding-base);
}
```

4.  Shell Provides Layout Context via SDK
    Inside window.FalconSDK.context, include:

```
context: {
  layout: {
    containerWidth: 'full' | 'boxed',
    padding: number,
    rtl: boolean,
  }
}
```

Micro-apps read it:

    `const layout = window.FalconSDK.context.layout;`

5.  Micro-App MUST NOT use their own Tailwind config for colors/layout

```
module.exports = {
  content: ['./src/**/*.{html,ts}'],
  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        primary: 'var(--primary-color)',
        secondary: 'var(--secondary-color)',
      },
    },
  },
  corePlugins: { preflight: false },  // prevents layout override
};
```

This ensures the micro-app and shell stay visually consistent.

